e Manager\nDescription: (Version 2503) To simplify navigation to your SAP BTP Cockpit and Dev Space Manager, we have added direct links in the Mobile Services cockpit.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-10\nValid as Of: 2025-04-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1064 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Full Initial Download from Offline Service\nDescription: (Version 2503) We've introduced a new feature labeled as Trigger Initial Download, this feature lets you initiate the full download of app data from the offline service and cancel the full initial download if needed. You can trigger this download from application level also registration level.For more information, see Managing App Users and Device Registrations and Defining Offline Settings for Applications.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-10\nValid as Of: 2025-04-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1065 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Include Predefined Annotations\nDescription: (Version 2503) We've introduced a new checkbox to enable predefined annotations for sample OData for testing.  For more information, see Using the Sample ODATA ESPM\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-10\nValid as Of: 2025-04-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1066 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Update: Logout Service\nDescription: (Version 2503) When the Logout API is called, it removes registrations for registered users and devices related with the push feature from the server.  For more information, see DELETE User Logout Request and POST User Logout Request.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-10\nValid as Of: 2025-04-10\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1067 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: Update to version 2.11.3\nDescription: We have implemented a watch mechanism to ensure that DNSEntry is up to date with the IP and host of the istio-ingressgateway service. Additionally, we've decreased the default reconciliation time to safeguard against possible scheduling errors.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-09\nValid as Of: 2025-04-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1068 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Feedback Option for Documentation\nDescription: You can now provide feedback on the SAP Task Center documentation using the Feedback  Comments function on the SAP Help Portal, without the need to use GitHub. You just need to log in to the SAP Help Portal with your email.   For more information, see Creating Better Documentation Together: SAP Help Portal’s new approach to Collaboration and Feedback.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-09\nValid as Of: 2025-04-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1069 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Identity Authentication (using SCIM API version 2) - changed behavior\nDescription: Similar to the Local Identity Directory, you can now use Identity Authentication (SCIM API version 2) for reading and writing application-specific groups. Depending on the configured pair of provisioning systems, to ensure successful provisioning, you might need to manually define value mappings for the attribute applicationId in the source or the target system transformations.  For more information, see:    Identity Authentication (Source)  Identity Authentication (Target)  List of Properties→ips.application.id  \nAction: Info only\",933\n166,\"--- Record 2401 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Copy Tasks\nDescription: You can now copy existing tasks to create new ones. This action offers an alternative to creating new tasks either from a model or manually.  More information:  How to Copy Tasks  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-02\nValid as Of: 2024-08-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2402 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Country/Region Assignments Displayed in Add Organizational Units Dialog\nDescription: You can now find the country/region assignment information in the Add Organizational Units dialog.  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-02\nValid as Of: 2024-08-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2403 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Editable Columns on Folder Level\nDescription: In the Tasks table on folder level, the columns for the different task attributes are now editable except for the Task Type column.  For user assignments, you can find additional columns. The combined columns for user and user group remain read-only. However, the new columns are individual columns for the user or user group respectively. In these columns, you can change the user assignments for the specific task without navigating to the task.  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-02\nValid as Of: 2024-08-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2404 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Metric Adjusted\nDescription: The metric used to count the number of company codes used has now been adjusted so that archived task lists are no longer considered.  More information:  SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-02\nValid as Of: 2024-08-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2405 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Read Authorization Added Automatically from the Beginning\nDescription: When a new user role is created, Read authorization is now added automatically from the beginning, since this is the minimum authorization required for a user role.  More information: See the underlying pages of Task List Creation Scope and Task Processing Scope.  App affected:  Manage User Roles\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-02\nValid as Of: 2024-08-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2406 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Table in Create Task from Model Dialog Improved\nDescription: In the Create Task from Model dialog, you can now find several additional columns providing more information. You can adjust the table using the Settings icon .  Additionally, you can now select several task models and this way create several tasks at once.  More information:  How to Create Tasks  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-02\nValid as Of: 2024-08-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2407 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Tables in Task Lists Adjusted\nDescription: The tables showing task lists in the Manage Closing Task Lists app have been adjusted to provide a better user experience. The Closing Type column isn't required for task lists and has been removed from the corresponding tables.  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists\nAction: Info only\nLifec